---
/*
 * The prompt mark — the `>_` beside the wordmark, as geometry rather than type.
 *
 * It was `<span>&gt;_</span>` — two unrelated glyphs from a proportional face,
 * so the chevron and the underscore sat on different baselines at different
 * optical weights and the pair read as disjointed beside a 700-weight
 * wordmark. Text also gave no way to size them relative to each other, or to
 * animate.
 *
 * As an SVG the two shapes are drawn to one grid, scale with the wordmark via
 * `em`, take their colour from `currentColor`, and the caret can blink the way
 * a real one does.
 *
 * ONE COPY, WHICH IS WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The same markup was inline in BOTH
 * `src/pages/index.astro` and `src/pages/profile.astro` — byte-identical path
 * data, with the explanation above written on the index copy only. So the
 * profile copy read as unexplained magic numbers, and any change to the
 * geometry had to be made twice with nothing to catch you if you made it once.
 * Both pages now render this component; there is no second copy to drift.
 *
 * It takes no props deliberately. It is a fixed mark, not a configurable icon.
 *
 * Presentation lives in `src/styles/hub.css` — `.hub__mark-icon` (sizing),
 * `.hub__mark-chevron` and `.hub__mark-caret` (fill, hover, the caret blink,
 * and the `[data-tmx-motion='reduce']` opt-out). This component carries no
 * <style> block, so those global rules still apply; adding one would scope the
 * classes and silently detach them.
 */
---

<svg class="hub__mark-icon" viewBox="0 0 34 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
	<path
		class="hub__mark-chevron"
		d="M3.4 4.2 L6.9 1.2 L18.4 12 L6.9 22.8 L3.4 19.8 L11.7 12 Z"
	/>
	<rect class="hub__mark-caret" x="20.5" y="18.4" width="11.5" height="3.4" rx="1.7" />
</svg>
